5. Training Objective and Manifold‑Freezing Curriculum

The total loss is a weighted sum with eight terms:

\begin{aligned}
\mathcal{L} = &\;\lambda_1\mathcal{L}_{\text{rec}}^{\text{nll}} + \lambda_2\mathcal{L}_{\text{dyn}} + \lambda_3\mathcal{L}_{\text{sparse}} + \lambda_4\mathcal{L}_{\text{S-MDL}} \\
&+ \lambda_5\mathcal{L}_{\text{stab}} + \lambda_6\mathcal{L}_{\text{causal}} + \lambda_7\mathcal{L}_{\text{UQ}} + \lambda_8\mathcal{L}_{\text{pin}},
\end{aligned}

where \mathcal{L}_{\text{rec}}^{\text{nll}} is the negative log‑likelihood under the ensemble Gaussian; \mathcal{L}_{\text{dyn}} is the MSE between encoded \dot{z} and g(z); \mathcal{L}_{\text{sparse}} is the ℓ₁ norm of coefficients; \mathcal{L}_{\text{stab}} is the Lyapunov penalty; and \mathcal{L}_{\text{UQ}} is a sharpness‑calibration penalty.

5.1 Three‑Phase Curriculum with Manifold Freezing

The most fragile moment in training is the simultaneous activation of Lyapunov stabilization and library expansion: the Lyapunov penalty pulls trajectories toward a stable equilibrium, while new candidate terms stretch the dynamics to fit residuals, causing destructive gradient interference. We eliminate this conflict by a manifold‑freezing protocol.

Phase 1 (Reconstruction + Dynamics). Only \mathcal{L}_{\text{rec}}, \mathcal{L}_{\text{dyn}}, \mathcal{L}_{\text{sparse}}, \mathcal{L}_{\text{pin}} are active. The encoder, decoder, and initial symbolic coefficients are trained to convergence, establishing a stable latent geometry.

Phase 2 (Stability + S‑MDL Expansion). The Lyapunov penalty \mathcal{L}_{\text{stab}} and S‑MDL regularisation are enabled. Library expansion is attempted when \bar{r} > \tau. Whenever an expansion is triggered:

1. Freeze the encoder and decoder weights entirely.
2. Add new candidate basis functions to \mathcal{L}; initialise their coefficients with small random values.
3. Train only the new coefficients (and existing coefficients via sparse regression) for N_{\text{warm}} epochs, keeping the latent manifold fixed.
4. Unfreeze all parameters and resume joint training.

This guarantees that new terms adapt to the existing latent geometry before the geometry itself can shift, preventing catastrophic interference.

Verification attempts follow the triggered protocol (Section 4.6): dReal counterexamples are generated every p epochs and used to update the safety buffer and Lyapunov network. Full α,β‑CROWN certification is executed only when the stability‑ready conditions are met.

Phase 3 (Causal + UQ). \mathcal{L}_{\text{causal}} and \mathcal{L}_{\text{UQ}} are switched on with small weights. The ensemble is trained, and split‑conformal calibration is applied. The final causal graph is extracted from the sparse coefficient matrix; if identity pinning is used, the first m nodes are physically labelled.

