7. Full Training Algorithm

The training procedure implements all the described safeguards. The following pseudocode summarises the algorithm.

---

Algorithm: ACKS‑WM Training with Manifold Freezing, S‑MDL Expansion, and Triggered Certification

1. Initialisation:
   · Encoder, decoder, \mathcal{L}_0, coefficients \Xi, \Xi^{\text{nl}}, lifted matrix A, Lyapunov net V_\phi, ensemble of 5 decoders.
   · Set S‑MDL parameters: expansion threshold \tau, noise‑rejection factor \kappa, MDL weights \alpha,\beta.
   · Set stability‑ready thresholds \epsilon_{\text{Lyap}}, \epsilon_{\text{inv}}, and verification interval p.
   · (Optional) Activate identity pinning for first m latent dimensions.
2. Phase 1 (Reconstruction + Dynamics + Pinning):
   · For E_1 epochs:
     · Encode history to z; compute \dot{z}.
     · Evaluate g(z); reconstruct field; compute losses.
     · Update encoder, decoder, \Xi (iterative thresholding) using \mathcal{L}_{\text{rec}}, \mathcal{L}_{\text{dyn}}, \mathcal{L}_{\text{sparse}}, \mathcal{L}_{\text{pin}}.
3. Phase 2 (Stability + S‑MDL Expansion + Barrier Sampling):
   · Initialise safety buffer \mathcal{B}=\varnothing, stability‑ready flag = false.
   · For E_2 epochs:
     · Expansion check: Compute \bar{r} and ensemble standard deviation \sigma_{\text{dyn}}.
       · If \bar{r} > \tau:
         · Generate candidate terms. Compute \Delta\bar{r} for each.
         · If \max \Delta\bar{r} > \kappa\sigma_{\text{dyn}}:
           1. Freeze encoder and decoder.
           2. Add best candidate term to \mathcal{L}; re‑compute mutual coherence \mu(\Phi).
           3. If \mu(\Phi) \ge 1/(2\hat{s}-1), abort expansion. Else:
              · Append new column to \Phi, initialise new \xi small.
              · Train only new coefficients for N_{\text{warm}} epochs.
           4. Unfreeze all weights. Update \hat{s} = \text{nnz}(\Xi)+1.
           5. Increment MDL weight \beta.
     · Lyapunov training: Train V_\phi using \mathcal{L}_{\text{stab}}. Every p epochs, run dReal on \mathcal{D}_k; add counterexamples to \mathcal{B} and training set.
     · Readiness check: Compute R_{\text{Lyap}} = \max_{z\in\mathcal{B}}(\dot{V}_\phi + \gamma V_\phi); update \sin\theta_1.
       · If R_{\text{Lyap}} < \epsilon_{\text{Lyap}} and \sin\theta_1 < \epsilon_{\text{inv}} and stability‑ready flag is false:
         · Set flag = true; launch α,β‑CROWN verification on \mathcal{D}_k.
         · If unsat, certificate is valid and stored. Else, additional counterexamples are added and flag reset.
   · Continue joint training.
4. Phase 3 (Causal + UQ):
   · For E_3 epochs:
     · Activate \mathcal{L}_{\text{causal}}: sample in silico soft shifts, compute invariance loss.
     · Activate \mathcal{L}_{\text{UQ}}; train ensemble members with different seeds.
   · Post‑training: split‑conformal calibration on held‑out set; extract causal graph from \Xi support; label pinned nodes by sensor index.
5. Output: Trained modules, symbolic dynamics g(z), causal DAG (with optional physical labels), verified Lyapunov function for subsystem, UQ predictor with coverage guarantee.

